# BTT Pi kiosk cron setup (10.0.0.230, user exoticos). Updated 2026-07-16.
#
# Two crontabs are used.

# ---- USER crontab  (crontab -e as exoticos) ----
# Watchdog every 2 min: relaunches / un-wedges Chromium (see kiosk-watchdog.sh).
*/2 * * * * /home/exoticos/kiosk-watchdog.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

# ---- ROOT crontab  (sudo crontab -e) ----
# Nightly FULL reboot at 04:00. A user cron can't reboot, so this lives in root's
# crontab. The reboot clears kernel-state creep on the BTT Armbian rk35xx kernel
# (recurring udev-worker Oops in kernfs_root + Bad rss-counter over long uptime),
# which a Chromium-only restart cannot clear. The kiosk auto-starts on boot via
# ~/.config/openbox/autostart -> kiosk.sh, and theengs.service resumes via systemd.
# This replaced the old 04:00 kiosk-restart.sh (Chromium-only) job.
0 4 * * * /sbin/reboot

# kiosk-restart.sh remains in this repo as a manual "clean Chromium restart" tool
# but is no longer wired to cron (the nightly reboot supersedes it).
